                    <div id="asyncQuestionOne"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#asyncQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            Asynchronous programming allows work to be started
                            without requiring the caller to wait synchronously
                            for that work to finish.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <!-- Q2 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-target="#asyncQuestionTwo">

                            What is CompletableFuture?

                        </button>

                    </h2>

                    <div id="asyncQuestionTwo"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#asyncQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            CompletableFuture represents a future result and
                            provides APIs for composing asynchronous stages,
                            handling results, and handling failures.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <!-- Q3 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-target="#asyncQuestionThree">

                            What is the difference between runAsync() and supplyAsync()?

                        </button>

                    </h2>

                    <div id="asyncQuestionThree"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#asyncQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            <code>runAsync()</code> performs an asynchronous
                            action without returning a result, while
                            <code>supplyAsync()</code> returns a result.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <!-- Q4 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-parent="#asyncQuestions"
                                data-bs-target="#asyncQuestionFour">

                            What is thenCompose()?

                        </button>

                    </h2>

                    <div id="asyncQuestionFour"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#asyncQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            <code>thenCompose()</code> chains dependent
                            asynchronous operations and avoids creating a
                            nested CompletableFuture.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <!-- Q5 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-target="#asyncQuestionFive">

                            What is thenCombine()?

                        </button>

                    </h2>

                    <div id="asyncQuestionFive"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#asyncQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            <code>thenCombine()</code> combines the results of
                            two independent CompletionStage computations.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <!-- Q6 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-target="#asyncQuestionSix">

                            How do you handle exceptions in CompletableFuture?

                        </button>

                    </h2>

                    <div id="asyncQuestionSix"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#asyncQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            Common methods include
                            <code>exceptionally()</code>,
                            <code>handle()</code>, and
                            <code>whenComplete()</code>.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <!-- Q7 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-target="#asyncQuestionSeven">

                            What is the difference between join() and get()?

                        </button>

                    </h2>

                    <div id="asyncQuestionSeven"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#asyncQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            Both wait for completion. <code>get()</code> uses
                            checked exceptions, while <code>join()</code>
                            reports failures using unchecked completion
                            exceptions.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <!-- Q8 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-target="#asyncQuestionEight">

                            What is allOf()?

                        </button>

                    </h2>

                    <div id="asyncQuestionEight"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#asyncQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            <code>allOf()</code> creates a completion stage
                            that completes when all supplied futures have
                            completed.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- SUMMARY -->
        <section class="mb-4">

            <div class="alert alert-primary border-0">

                <h5 class="fw-bold">
                    Summary
                </h5>

                <p class="mb-0">
                    Java asynchronous programming provides APIs for starting,
                    composing, combining, and handling asynchronous tasks.
                    CompletableFuture is central to this model, with methods
                    such as runAsync, supplyAsync, thenApply, thenCompose,
                    thenCombine, allOf, anyOf, exceptionally, handle, and
                    whenComplete.
                </p>

            </div>

        </section>


